1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,516
Chapter seven. Doctor X.

2
00:00:02,866 --> 00:00:09,743
And what about Farnsworth? He never got rich from television. His early patents expired just as the industry took off.

3
00:00:09,943 --> 00:00:15,257
According to his son, he disliked what was being broadcast. He didn't want his children watching it.

4
00:00:15,457 --> 00:00:25,057
In 1957, he was invited onto a television quiz show where celebrities had to guess a guest's secret. He was introduced as Doctor X.

5
00:00:25,257 --> 00:00:30,527
Viewers at home read his secret on the screen: he had invented electronic television.

6
00:00:30,727 --> 00:00:42,738
The panelists asked everything. They couldn't guess. The host told him that without him, he would be out of a job. Farnsworth walked away with eighty dollars and a carton of cigarettes.

7
00:00:43,638 --> 00:00:49,622
The inventor of television appeared on television. And nobody recognized him.
